{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7senopyjprjr5vsr7agqagjhqyqaq756smg4g3dso5kmk7bhgyla","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `c_src/` is untouched (all mtimes are the original 16:42 checkout time), and the translation builds clean with `cargo build --release` (zero warnings).\n\n## Artifacts\n\n| File | Lines | Contents |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Cargo.toml` | — | bin target `driver`, edition 2021, no dependencies |\n| `src/cio.rs` | 372 | C-stdio compatibility layer |\n| `src/shape.rs` | 290 | `shape.c` / `shape.h` |\n| `src/scene.rs` | 218 | `scene.c` / `scene.h` |\n| `src/main.rs` | 529 | `main.c` (menu loop + all 12 commands) |\n| `dev_tests/{compare,fuzz}.py` | — | differential test harnesses I used for verification |\n\n## Fidelity details that needed care\n\n- **stdout buffering**: `Out` reimplements a glibc `FILE*` — fills a 4096-byte buffer completely before each `write(2)`, never flushes before reading stdin (fully buffered), and switches to line buffering when stdout is a tty. This makes even *partial* output on an abnormal exit byte-identical.\n- **`scanf` vs `fgets`**: `scanf(\"%d\")` skips whitespace across newlines; `fgets` stops at a newline and leaves overlong lines to be read as the next \"line\". Both modeled on a shared byte stream with sticky EOF, as in C.\n- **Reproduced bug**: `while (getchar() != '\\n');` never terminates once stdin is at EOF. The Rust version also never returns, and (like C) leaves its stdout buffer unflushed — verified to produce identical partial output (0 B, 4096 B, 24576 B cases).\n- **`%d` overflow**: mimics glibc's strtol clamp-to-`LONG_MIN/MAX` then truncate-to-`int` (e.g. `99999999999999999999` → same value as C).\n- **`%p`**: unmatchable by construction; shapes get deterministic synthetic addresses (`0x…` lowercase, one 0x9a0 glibc chunk apart, matching `sizeof(shape_t)`), preserving pointer *identity* relationships.\n- **Raw bytes**: scene names/filenames are `Vec<u8>`, so non-UTF-8 input, embedded NULs, `strcspn`/`strncpy` truncation at 63 bytes, and non-UTF-8 filenames all behave exactly as in C.\n\n## Verification (my own, on disk)\n\n- 51 hand-built differential cases comparing **stdout, stderr, exit code, and files written**: `0 failure(s) out of 51`.\n- 400 randomized fuzz trials (including EOF-hang inputs): `0 failures / 400 trials`.\n- Binary-byte tests for non-UTF-8/NUL names and filenames: stdout, stderr, and the saved scene file all identical."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":446,"cache_read_input_tokens":89808,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":446,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c82c739-fc36-46a5-a7c4-6b822a9fa6ed","uuid":"df3f2eba-2ed9-4174-b201-f5bd16783d61","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:55:52.161Z"}
